############ PART 1: kubesec, every Deployment scored separately
The earlier audit piped whole manifests to 'scan /dev/stdin', which reads only the first
YAML document. For 30-services.yaml that meant pricing-fn alone was ever scored.
Here each Deployment is exported from the cluster and scored on its own, so the score
describes what is actually running rather than what a file claims.

  checkout-fn    score=12   not satisfied: ApparmorAny SeccompAny RunAsGroup RunAsUser 
  gateway        score=12   not satisfied: ApparmorAny SeccompAny RunAsGroup RunAsUser 
  inventory-fn   score=12   not satisfied: ApparmorAny SeccompAny RunAsGroup RunAsUser 
  postgres       score=11   not satisfied: ApparmorAny SeccompAny RunAsGroup RunAsUser ReadOnlyRootFilesystem 
  pricing-fn     score=12   not satisfied: ApparmorAny SeccompAny RunAsGroup RunAsUser 

  Deployments found: 5, scored: 5

  Note on SeccompAny: kubesec's selector for that rule is the deprecated annotation
  container.seccomp.security.alpha.kubernetes.io/pod. Every workload here sets the
  current field instead, so the rule is a false negative. Proof, straight from the API:
    checkout-fn seccompProfile=RuntimeDefault
    gateway seccompProfile=RuntimeDefault
    inventory-fn seccompProfile=RuntimeDefault
    postgres seccompProfile=RuntimeDefault
    pricing-fn seccompProfile=RuntimeDefault

